# Two threads keep their own 287 states (roadmap l4.md L2, D17): the program
# keeps pi, the counter at the same priority keeps 1, and the time slices
# switch the 287 between them, lazily, many times. MAME has no 287, and
# DOSBox-X ignores TS (docs/emulators.md).
program: fputhreads
emulators: bochs
define: TEST_COUNTER_SAME
define: TEST_COUNTER_FPU
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
---
rx286, test build
program: its 287 state kept
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread program ran
rx286: thread counter ran
